{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-97413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-97413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18+8+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-97413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b3dde96a478b61d719fd518dcbfe870937305ab4a3d5e1e2ed43ec4aebbdce6"} {"question" "q-97413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-97413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices"