"value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b3dde96a478b61d719fd518dcbfe870937305ab4a3d5e1e2ed43ec4aebbdce6"} {"question" "q-42714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-42714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{14}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-42714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-141167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2-t+{t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-141167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2-t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=2,\\,p(2)=4,\\,p(3)=8.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{84} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-141167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b3dde96a478b61d719fd518dcbfe870937305ab4a3d5e1e2ed43ec4aebbdce6"} {"question" "q-141167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-141167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{21}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{14}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{21}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-141167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{21}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-97425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=5-3t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-97425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=5-3t,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=5,\\,p(2)=-1,\\,p(3)=-4.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8eb6d9e26d862ba71181b65bd1572d54a9581dc2b38faadc8fb0aaebd83ddcb"} {"question" "q-97425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b3dde96a478b61d719fd518dcbfe870937305ab4a3d5e1e2ed43ec4aebbdc